    "profile_text": {
        "body": "CrowdStrike is a global cybersecurity company that describes itself as an AI-native provider focused on stopping breaches. Its cloud-native Falcon platform is designed to protect endpoints, cloud workloads, identities, and data, combining what the company describes as security data, AI intelligence, automation, and expert services. The company also references an initiative called Project QuiltWorks, which it says expands its data partnerships across the technology ecosystem to address risks from frontier AI.\n\nCrowdStrike's primary AI product is Charlotte AI, categorized as a security operations tool covering threat detection, autonomous response, and high-privilege access management. The Falcon platform more broadly incorporates AI model scanning and an AI security dashboard for securing cloud environments, and the company positions it as a defense against adversaries who use AI to accelerate attacks.\n\nCrowdStrike is a publicly traded company listed on Nasdaq under the ticker CRWD, with SEC CIK 0001535527. No litigation or MCP server registrations are recorded in the current held facts.",
